      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg of ibuprofen four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for an adult.\n\n- **Per dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg. Doses above that add little benefit and more risk.\n- **Per day:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. Most clinicians use less for inpatients, and OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at 6,400 mg/day:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, fluid retention, hypertension, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? These are some common intended regimens:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give your rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
     ],
